2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"828\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:828,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:300691,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/173350728?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!nRYm!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F3f284ea2-e0e8-4003-9da6-f0b8ab40434b_1678x954.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Which totals 49.</p><p>And, for a minute, in the good old US of A, that number is…503 just last year.  This is 10x higher than all of the previous century in Australia, and 100x higher than the last century in Japan.</p><p>I’m not even trying to claim that this is utter insanity; I’m pointing out something much simpler—children <em>notice</em>.</p><p>My children, your children, Mr. Kirk’s children, will all have an <em>opinion</em>.  They are judging us, our actions, and how we choose to protect them or protect their other rights via the relentless arming of an occasionally unhinged and unstable citizenry, a tiny fraction of which has decided, on repeat, to kill them, their classmates, even their favorite Second Amendment enthusiasts.</p><p>Our children judge what they see, and judge what we do.  If they think we don’t care about their lives?  They are correct.  We, in America, have made a choice to privilege the <em>ease of would-be gunmen with murderous conviction</em> over their right, on par with gun ownership, of children to stay alive.</p><p>Our children, I fear, will judge us harshly for the choices we’ve made.  When you tuck your kids in at night and imagine, years from now, in your dotage, when they are considering what old folks home to plop you in…what do you want them to remember?</p><p>Did we protect children?  Or did we protect the gunmen’s grim workflow?</p><p>Ethical principles, and indeed, rights, are always in conflict.  We always make trade-offs.</p><p>I pray we choose more wisely.</p><p>Charlie—rest in peace, my friend.  He, at least, chose debate and engagement, a choice every American should <em>honor</em>.   His murder deserves no such consideration, and I hope he sleeps poorly ever onward. I wish him due process, and nothing more.</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/in-other-news-more-people-are-shot?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/in-other-news-more-people-are-shot?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><div class=\"pullquote\"><p><a href=\"https://www.meetradial.com/blog/is-ptsd-curable\">Learn more about healing from PTSD at Radial</a></p></div><p></p><p>  </p><p></p>","text":"Being shot to death is the leading cause of death among children in America. He’s a map of just shootings with a child involved...\n\nActivists like the late Charlie Kirk were fond of pointing out that those statistics, as reported NEJM and in the Journal “Pediatrics” by Lee et. al. , include older youth, as if this somehow makes it better:\n\nFirearms are the leading cause of death in children and youth 0 to 24 years of age in the United States.\n\nFor the next generation of master debaters, here are the supplemental materials that can help you spin this data any which way you’d like, such as highlighting how many youth were black, if you're inclined to discount some lives over others based on the color of the skin of the child whose family is left to mourn their passing (from NEJM, 2022):\n\nAnd to remind us all how many school shootings there are, and what the trend looks like, here is a graph from the K-12 shooting database :\n\nIn case it’s not clear, the numbers are going up. The late Mr. Kirk was a master debater (recently parodied— with enthusiastic support by Charlie himself — on South Park, and as yesterday ago, pulled off the internet by Paramount ), and would often counter questions about gun violence by pointing out that children up to age 24 are barely children at all. They are still dead, though, after being shot by a gun.\n\nMr. Kirk was murdered, with a gun, by what I can only assume is a giant a-hole, on a college campus. His number won’t be added to that K-12 number .\n\nMr. Kirk was correct to note that the cost of having a well-armed populace is excess deaths . In 2023, at one of his own events, he weighed in on the fact that these deaths are a price we should be willing to pay :\n\nTurning Point USA CEO and co-founder Charlie Kirk said of gun deaths on April 5, 2023, \" I think it's worth it. I think it's worth to have a cost of, unfortunately, some gun deaths every single year so that we can have the Second Amendment to protect our other God-given rights.\"\n\nTo be clear, the only way in which gun ownership protects our other god given rights is by granting anyone with temerity the opportunity to end the lives of those with whom they disagree, absent due process or judicial review.\n\nI’m not cheering for the death of Mr. Kirk—quite the opposite. I oppose gun violence. I oppose political violence. I oppose corporate violence. This excess death is a bad plan and a bad deal, is my debating point. Mr. Kirk had every right to advocate for his views. One of those views is that the following map of mass shootings over the past 11 years is a price we get right with god about :\n\nMr. Kirk and his co-enthusiasts for the Second Amendment can hold any belief and advocate for it. Again, Mr. Kirk’s stance:\n\n“ I think it's worth to have a cost of, unfortunately, some gun deaths every single year so that we can have the Second Amendment to protect our other God-given rights.\"\n\nAs a pediatric subspecialist, I have a different opinion. I’m not going to shoot you about it—unlike the craven who chose his “rights” over Mr. Kirk’s life— I am going to try to persuade you.\n\nA comparison might be helpful? Here is the list of every single mass shooting in Japan in the 21st century\n\nThat is a total of… 15 between 2007 and 2023.\n\nWe don’t need a visualizer on a map of Japan to display that.\n\nHere is every 21st-century mass shooting in Australia:\n\nWhich totals 49.\n\nAnd, for a minute, in the good old US of A, that number is…503 just last year. This is 10x higher than all of the previous century in Australia, and 100x higher than the last century in Japan.\n\nI’m not even trying to claim that this is utter insanity; I’m pointing out something much simpler—children notice .\n\nMy children, your children, Mr. Kirk’s children, will all have an opinion . They are judging us, our actions, and how we choose to protect them or protect their other rights via the relentless arming of an occasionally unhinged and unstable citizenry, a tiny fraction of which has decided, on repeat, to kill them, their classmates, even their favorite Second Amendment enthusiasts.\n\nOur children judge what they see, and judge what we do. If they think we don’t care about their lives? They are correct. We, in America, have made a choice to privilege the ease of would-be gunmen with murderous conviction over their right, on par with gun ownership, of children to stay alive.\n\nOur children, I fear, will judge us harshly for the choices we’ve made. When you tuck your kids in at night and imagine, years from now, in your dotage, when they are considering what old folks home to plop you in…what do you want them to remember?\n\nDid we protect children? Or did we protect the gunmen’s grim workflow?\n\nEthical principles, and indeed, rights, are always in conflict. We always make trade-offs.\n\nI pray we choose more wisely.\n\nCharlie—rest in peace, my friend. He, at least, chose debate and engagement, a choice every American should honor . His murder deserves no such consideration, and I hope he sleeps poorly ever onward. I wish him due process, and nothing more.\n\nShare\n\nSubscribe now\n\nLearn more about healing from PTSD at Radial"}